# std.net over loopback: listener options, stream options and addresses, a half-close, net.Conn,
# a Unix-domain socket (named relative to the run directory on Windows, else in the system
# temporary directory), an Accept cut by a deadline, refusals.
# The timeout is wide for a loaded Windows host, where a dial to a closed port can wait seconds
# for the refusal.
case ok
stdout sockets.out
timeout 120
